---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { brand } from "../content/siteCopy";
---

<Base
	title="Resources"
	description="Guidance on Virginia Medicaid waivers (FIS, BI, CL), referrals, accessibility, and transportation for Autism Sanctuary."
>
	<section class="page-banner">
		<div class="container">
			<span class="eyebrow">Resources &amp; guidance</span>
			<h1>Funding, referrals, and getting here—without the jargon storm.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				This page summarizes common pathways families and case managers use when exploring supports. It is
				informational, not legal advice.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-cream">
		<div class="container prose-wide" style="margin:0 auto;">
			<h2>Referral &amp; application pathway</h2>
			<ol class="checklist" style="list-style:decimal;">
				<li><strong>Review programs:</strong> Read <a href="/programs">Programs</a>.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Contact admissions:</strong> Email
					<a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}>{brand.email}</a> or call
					<a href={brand.phoneHref}>{brand.phone}</a>.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Complete intake:</strong> Start via <a href="/admissions">Admissions</a>.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Plan authorization:</strong> We coordinate with case managers and CSBs to confirm funding
					alignment.
				</li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container" style="max-width:44rem;">
			<span class="eyebrow">Funding frameworks (Virginia)</span>
			<h2>Waivers and individualized authorization</h2>
			<article class="feature-block">
				<h3>Medicaid waivers (overview)</h3>
				<p>
					Many people access services through Virginia’s Medicaid waiver programs—commonly Family &amp;
					Individual Supports (FIS), Building Independence (BI), and Community Living (CL). Each has distinct
					eligibility rules, budgets, and service definitions.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Your case manager</strong> determines whether a specific Autism Sanctuary service can be
					authorized on an ISP.
				</p>
				<div class="note">
					<strong>Heads-up:</strong> Autism Sanctuary does not coordinate Children’s Services Act (CSA)
					funding. If CSA is part of your conversation, your case manager can help identify appropriate
					providers.
				</div>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-meadow">
		<div class="container split">
			<div class="stack prose-wide">
				<span class="eyebrow">Accessibility &amp; transportation</span>
				<h2>Inclusive access within a working farm.</h2>
				<p>
					Trails, gardens, and program buildings are checked for safe use; individualized plans may include
					adaptive equipment, pacing, or alternative activities when weather or terrain shifts.
				</p>
				<p>
					Transportation arrangements vary; talk with admissions about how people typically arrive and what
					supports are realistic for your situation.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="media-frame">
				<img
					src="/media/farm-detail.jpg"
					alt="Detail of outdoor farm environment at Autism Sanctuary."
					width="1200"
					height="900"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
				/>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<CtaBand
		title="Questions about funding or access?"
		primaryHref="/contact?intent=program-fit"
		primaryLabel="Send an inquiry"
		secondaryHref="/admissions"
		secondaryLabel="Admissions"
	/>
</Base>
